## Problem

The existing tests cover individual functions in isolation but there is no single end-to-end integration test that walks through a complete, successful raffle lifecycle.

## Required Test

```rust
#[test]
fn full_lifecycle_happy_path() {
    let env = Env::default();
    env.mock_all_auths();
    env.ledger().set_timestamp(1000);

    // 1. Deploy factory and register raffle WASM
    // 2. Init factory
    // 3. Creator calls create_raffle
    // 4. Creator deposits prize
    // 5. Three buyers purchase tickets
    // 6. Creator calls finalize_raffle (after end time)
    // 7. Verify winner is one of the three buyers
    // 8. Advance past claim lockup
    // 9. Winner claims prize
    // 10. Verify winner's balance increased by net_prize
    // 11. Verify raffle status == Claimed
    // 12. Verify protocol fee reached treasury

    // Assert invariant: total_distributed == prize_amount - protocol_fees
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Test covers the complete happy path from factory init to prize claim
- [ ] Verifies token balance changes at every step
- [ ] Verifies raffle status transitions at every step
- [ ] Verifies events emitted at every step
- [ ] Test is in `contracts/raffle-instance/src/test.rs`

# Blacklisted winner will block the other winner's prize.

### Severity
High Risk

### Relevant GitHub Links
<a data-meta="codehawks-github-link" href="https://github.com/Cyfrin/2023-08-sparkn/blob/main/src/Distributor.sol#L147">https://github.com/Cyfrin/2023-08-sparkn/blob/main/src/Distributor.sol#L147</a>


## Summary
`Distributor._distribute()` will distribute prize to winners.

If any of the transfer fails, e.g USDC blacklisting, a whole transaction will revert.

## Vulnerability Details
```solidity
        uint256 winnersLength = winners.length; // cache length
        for (uint256 i; i < winnersLength;) {
            uint256 amount = totalAmount * percentages[i] / BASIS_POINTS;
            erc20.safeTransfer(winners[i], amount); // @audit - any of the winner is blacklisted.
            unchecked {
                ++i;
            }
        }
```

## Impact
DoS of Prize distribution

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommendations
Should have claim() function where winners can withdraw their prize.

```solidity
+   mapping(address => uint256) public prize;
+   IERC20 public prizeToken;

+   function claimPrize() external {
+       uint256 amount = prize[msg.sender];
+       if (amount > 0)
+       {
+           delete prize[msg.sender];
+           prizeToken.safeTransfer(msg.sender, amount);
+       }
+   }
```

